<title>INDIA: India repo auction cut-off falls to 3.5 pct.</title>
<headline>India repo auction cut-off falls to 3.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Tuesday it set a cut-off of 3.5 percent at its five-day repo auction of government securities against 4.0 percent at the last auction.</p>
<p>The RBI said it received 79 bids for 110.40 billion rupees of which it accepted 29 for 42.67 billion.</p>
<p>The weighted-average cut-off was 3.3597 percent, it said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
